      "claim": "Kitchen‑grade tin (aluminum) foil is a thin conductive sheet about 16 µm thick.",
      "evidence": "Commercial aluminum foil specifications list thickness ≈0.016 mm (16 µm). Conductivity of aluminum ≈3.5×10⁷ S/m.",
